1
00:00:00,186 --> 00:00:07,567
(Q31（单选）) Good morning. In the last few lectures I've been talking about the history of domestic building construction.

2
00:00:07,567 --> 00:00:14,016
But today I want to begin looking at some contemporary, experimental designs for housing.

3
00:00:14,016 --> 00:00:21,494
So, I'm going to start with a house which is constructed more or less under the ground.

4
00:00:21,494 --> 00:00:35,729
[Q31-C干扰项] And one of the interesting things about this project is that the owners-both professionals but not architects-wanted to be closely involved, So they decided to manage the project themselves.

5
00:00:35,729 --> 00:00:43,863
[Q31答案句] Their chief aim was to create somewhere that was as environmentally-friendly as possible.

6
00:00:43,863 --> 00:00:54,110
[Q31-A 干扰项] But at the same time they wanted to live somewhere peaceful-they'd both grown up in a rural area and disliked urban life.

7
00:00:54,110 --> 00:01:03,433
(Q32) So the first thing they did was to look for a site. And they found a disused stone quarry in a beautiful area.

8
00:01:03,433 --> 00:01:10,792
[Q32答案句] The price was relatively low, and they liked the idea of recycling the land, as it were.

9
00:01:10,792 --> 00:01:19,567
As it was, the quarry was an ugly blot on the landscape, and it wasn't productive any longer, either.

10
00:01:19,567 --> 00:01:28,389
(Q33（notes填空）) They consulted various architects and looked at a number of designs before finally deciding on one.

11
00:01:28,389 --> 00:01:39,619
As I've said, it was a design for a sort of underground house, and it was built into the earth itself, with two storeys.

12
00:01:39,619 --> 00:01:50,452
The north, east and west sides were set in the earth, and only the sloping, south-facing side was exposed to light.

13
00:01:50,452 --> 00:01:55,911
[Q33答案句] That was made of a double layer of very strong glass.

14
00:01:55,911 --> 00:02:03,684
(Q34) There were also photovoltaic tiles fixed to the top and bottom of this sloping wall.

15
00:02:03,684 --> 00:02:08,973
These are tiles that are designed to store energy from the sun.

16
00:02:08,973 --> 00:02:15,205
[Q34答案句] And the walls had a layer of foam around them too, to increase the insulation.

17
00:02:15,205 --> 00:02:23,487
(Q35) Now, what is of interest to us about this project is the features which make the building energy-efficient.

18
00:02:23,487 --> 00:02:32,911
[Q35答案句] Sunlight floods in through the glass wall, and to maximise it there are lots of mirrors and windows inside the house.

19
00:02:32,911 --> 00:02:41,227
(Q36) That helps to spread the light around. So that's the first thing - light is utilised as fully as possible.

20
00:02:41,227 --> 00:02:50,657
In addition, the special tiles on the outside convert energy from the sun and generate some of the house's electricity.

21
00:02:50,657 --> 00:03:04,241
[Q36答案句] In fact, and it's possible that in future the house may even generate an electricity surplus, and that the owners will be able to sell some to the national grid.

22
00:03:04,241 --> 00:03:10,962
(Q37) As well as that, wherever possible, recycled materials have been used.

23
00:03:10,962 --> 00:03:15,947
[Q37答案句] For example, the floors are made of reclaimed wood.

24
00:03:15,947 --> 00:03:24,071
(Q38) And the owners haven't bought a single item of new furniture-they just kept what they already had.

25
00:03:24,071 --> 00:03:29,163
[Q38答案句] And then there's the system for dealing with the waste produced in the house.

26
00:03:29,163 --> 00:03:39,921
(Q39) This is dealt with organically - it's purified by being filtered through reed beds which have been planted for that purpose in the garden.

27
00:03:39,921 --> 00:03:47,178
So the occupants of the house won't pollute the land or use any damaging chemicals.

28
00:03:47,178 --> 00:03:53,891
It's true that the actual construction of the house was harmful to the environment.

29
00:03:53,891 --> 00:04:03,493
[Q39答案句] Mainly because they had to use massive amounts of concrete - one of the biggest sources of carbon dioxide in manufacturing.

30
00:04:03,493 --> 00:04:09,290
(Q40) And, as you know, this is very damaging to the environment.

31
00:04:09,290 --> 00:04:20,297
In total, the house construction has released 70 tons of carbon dioxide into the air. Now that's a frightening thought.

32
00:04:20,297 --> 00:04:29,564
[Q40答案句] However, once the initial 'debt' has been cleared - and it's been calculated that this will only take fifteen years -

33
00:04:29,564 --> 00:04:42,954
this underground house won't cost anything - environmentally I mean - because unlike ordinary houses, it is run in a way that is completely environmentally friendly.

34
00:04:42,954 --> 00:04:45,454
So, eco-housing like this is likely to become much more…

